TSDRPlugin_SDRPlay - SDRplay RSP support for TempestSDR
=======================================================

This plugin gives TempestSDR access to SDRplay RSP receivers through the
legacy SDRplay "Mirics" API (mir_sdr_api.dll v2.13). It supports:

  * RSP1 (original)
  * early RSP2 / "RSPII" development hardware
  * macOS (via the mirsdrapi-rsp library)

Modern SDRplay receivers (RSP1A, RSPdx, RSPduo, ...) use the newer
sdrplay_api and are NOT supported by this plugin. For those, use the
TSDRPlugin_ExtIO plugin together with SDRplay's ExtIO_RSP.dll instead.

Building
--------

No SDRplay SDK is required to build this plugin. The matching API header
(src/mir_sdr.h, Mirics API v2.13) is vendored in the repository and the API
is loaded dynamically at runtime, so the plugin links against nothing but the
standard Windows/macOS system libraries.

On Windows, build together with the Java GUI (from JavaGUI/):

    make all ARCHNAME=X64

The resulting TSDRPlugin_SDRPlay.dll is copied to JavaGUI/lib/WINDOWS/X64.

Runtime requirements (Windows)
-----------------------------

The plugin loads mir_sdr_api.dll (legacy v2.13) at runtime. It is searched:

  1. on the standard Windows library search path (System32 is the default
     location used by the SDRplay RSP1/RSP2 driver installer; the current
     directory, i.e. the folder you launch TempestSDR from, is also searched),
     and
  2. in the folder that contains TSDRPlugin_SDRPlay.dll itself.

So either:

  * install the SDRplay RSP1/RSP2 driver package (which puts the API into
    System32), or
  * copy mir_sdr_api.dll (v2.13, 64-bit for an X64 build) into the folder you
    launch TempestSDR from (e.g. JavaGUI/, next to JTempestSDR.jar), or into
    the folder that contains TSDRPlugin_SDRPlay.dll.

The driver can be obtained from the SDRplay website (https://www.sdrplay.com/)
- legacy RSP1 API section. If mir_sdr_api.dll can not be found, loading the
plugin fails with a clear message pointing to this file.